{"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"axios.com/2026/09/26/ope…","end":681,"expanded_url":"https://www.axios.com/2026/09/26/openai-anthropic-thousands-ai-security-incidents","start":658,"url":"https://t.co/42h9aR4sem"}]},"text":"SCOOP: OpenAI, Anthropic and security researchers are investigating tens of thousands of incidents - not dozens - in which their frontier models took steps that outside evaluators would consider problematic, sources told Axios.\n\nThe sheer volume of incidents found in our reporting indicate that the problem is orders of magnitude more complex than what is currently publicly known and disclosed.\n\nThe findings also raise questions about what level of control anyone working on AI development can expect to have over their own technology, and whether these kinds of incidents are becoming synonymous with frontier deployment.\n\nRead my latest for Axios here: https://t.co/42h9aR4sem"},"created_at":"2026-09-26T22:40:29.000Z","conversation_id":"2103978039097037144","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2103978039097037144"]},"urls":[{"field":"note_tweet.entities","url":"https://t.co/42h9aR4sem","expandedUrl":"https://www.axios.com/2026/09/26/openai-anthropic-thousands-ai-security-incidents","displayUrl":"axios.com/2026/09/26/ope…","start":658,"end":681}],"references":[]}}]}},"source":{"version":1,"url":"https://x.com/i/web/status/2104069721532571971","textField":"text","raw":{"text":"RT @mehdirhasan: Insane that we allow this. Sleepwalking into disaster or worse","entities":{"mentions":[{"end":15,"id":"130557513","start":3,"username":"mehdirhasan"}]},"created_at":"2026-09-27T04:44:47.000Z","conversation_id":"2104069721532571971","referenced_tweets":[{"id":"2103996584484642894","type":"retweeted"}],"edit_history_tweet_ids":["2104069721532571971"]},"urls":[],"references":[{"id":"2103996584484642894","type":"retweeted","url":"https://x.com/i/web/status/2103996584484642894","createdAt":"2026-09-26T23:54:10.000Z","source":{"version":1,"url":"https://x.com/i/web/st